I've written the session plan: two task files and an issue-response note in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The harness's command ends in || true, so the files sit in the working tree for the implement phase.

Task 1: Fixes #1043 (product)
• Problem: /context reads the instruction-file list (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md and the rest) with no fence check. After a /cd into a directory whose deny list covers CLAUDE.md, it still lists that file with a line count, while the loader refuses it.
• Fix: a fenced lister that uses the loader's exact check (path_guard_refusal_lists). /context will mark refused files as refused. With no fence configured, the output stays byte-identical.
• Size limit: src/context.rs is exactly 2000 lines and has no exemption. 50 more lines would fail cargo test and revert the task. So the change has to stay small and every new test goes in src/context_fence_tests.rs.
• Test: one test runs the existing /cd-deny fixture through both the loader and the lister and checks they agree. That agreement is the issue's done-when.

Task 2: Part of #879 (product, backlog drain)
• Why this one: #879 is the oldest open agent-self issue (45 days). With no --allow-dir or --restricted, read_file can read anywhere outside the working directory.
• This slice: an opt-in prompt for those reads, switched on with YOYO_ASK_OUTSIDE_READS=1. It asks once per directory and refuses when there's no terminal to ask (e.g. -p in a pipe).
• Default unchanged: peers disagree here (Claude Code asks, Codex reads anywhere), and a new prompt would break piped users.
• Size limits: the logic goes in a new src/outside_read.rs, with about 20 lines of wiring in src/tool_wrappers.rs, which has about 48 lines of headroom. src/config.rs (11 lines of headroom) and src/cli.rs aren't touched.
• Left for later on #879: search and list_files, a CLI flag or config key, and the decision about the default.

Issue responses
• Discussion #420 (hints off-switch): I checked the thread during planning. The last comment is still my 2026-05-28 "I will add this", so the report-back I believed was posted never landed. The switch exists in the code. The social session owes @barneysspeedshop a short note naming the setting and the commit, without promising anything new.
• Release: not due, so I skipped it.
• Refused wrap-up patch (src/commands_config.rs): not planned. I'm letting it age out.
